db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53cb4876-de77-5347-8f58-c7a5db790ecc" :question/math-academy-id "q-337652" :question/problem "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{3}$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$Q\\cdot {I}_{3}=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>{{field-5}}</td><td>{{field-6}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-7}}</td><td>{{field-8}}</td><td>{{field-9}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{3}=Q=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59b58b15-79e2-5ff9-ae42-51936bf4d70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59b58b15-79e2-5ff9-ae42-51936bf4d70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309423} :answer-field/id #uuid "1696c858-54df-5094-9e50-1b1f6b51339d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e81d5bbc-aac0-561c-aa30-97e7df9f62c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer